-- title:
--   Hopf kernel of the quotient by a Hopf subalgebra's augmentation ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $H$ a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $k$ which is of finite type as a $k$-algebra. Let $K$ be a $k$-subalgebra of $H$ subject to two closure conditions: for every $x \in K$ the comultiplication $\Delta(x)$ lies in the $k$-submodule of $H \otimes_k H$ spanned by the elementary tensors $a \otimes b$ with $a, b \in K$, and the antipode of $H$ maps $K$ into $K$. Let $B$ be a commutative ring with a $k$-bialgebra structure and let $q \colon H \to B$ be a $k$-bialgebra homomorphism which is surjective as a function and whose kernel, as a ring homomorphism, equals the ideal of $H$ generated by the set $\{x \in K \mid \varepsilon(x) = 0\}$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit of $H$. The conclusion is an equality of $k$-subalgebras of $H$: the subalgebra $\mathrm{hopfKer}\,q$, defined as the equaliser of the two $k$-algebra maps $H \to H \otimes_k B$ given by $\Delta$ followed by $\mathrm{id}_H \otimes q$ and by $h \mapsto h \otimes 1$, is equal to $K$; that is, $\{h \in H \mid (\mathrm{id} \otimes q)\Delta(h) = h \otimes 1\} = K$.
--
--   This is one direction of Takeuchi's correspondence between Hopf subalgebras and normal Hopf ideals of a commutative Hopf algebra: geometrically, for $N = \operatorname{Spec}(H/K^{+}H)$ inside $G = \operatorname{Spec} H$, the $N$-invariant functions on $G$ are exactly $K = \mathcal{O}(G/N)$. It feeds the rank computation [`HopfAlgebra.finrank_eq_finrank_quotient_map_ker_counit_mul_finrank_range`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.finrank_eq_finrank_quotient_map_ker_counit_mul_finrank_range) and the surjectivity-and-exactness statement for Dieudonné modules used in the deformation-theoretic part of the development.
